.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH kakashi-observe 1  "observe " 
.SH NAME
kakashi\-observe \- Run one confined invocation of `program` and record it as an experiment (§6, §13)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkakashi observe\fR [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-watch\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROGRAM\fR> [\fIARGS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run one confined invocation of `program` and record it as an experiment (§6, §13)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR [default: .]
Directory containing (or to contain) the `.kakashi/` state directory (§34)
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-secs\fR \fI<TIMEOUT_SECS>\fR [default: 10]

.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-watch\-dir\fR \fI<WATCH_DIR>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROGRAM\fR>

.TP
[\fIARGS\fR]

